         <head>After Two Nights of the Ear-Ache</head>
         <author>By FRANCIS HARD</author>
         <pb/>
         <div type="div1">
            <head>After Two Nights of the Ear-ache</head>
            <p rend="justify">[Transcriber Note: This etext was produced from Weird Tales October 1937. Extensive research did not uncover any evidence that the U.S. copyright on this publication was renewed.]</p>
            <lg>
               <l>Most gentle Sleep! Two nights I wooed in vain;</l>
               <l>  Thou wouldst not come to banish racking pain:</l>
               <l>  For what is Sleep but Life in stone bound fast?</l>
               <l>  Oblivion of the Present, Future, Past.</l>
            </lg>
         </div>
